				368,
				3
			],
			"Message": "docs(Common): Replace literal em spaces with HTML numeric entity in markdown\n\nGitHub-flavored Markdown handles literal Unicode em spaces (U+2001) inconsistently across browsers and renderers, causing visual alignment breakage in headers, table cells, and diagram labels. Replace all `\\u2001` characters with the `&#x2001;` HTML numeric entity, which renders reliably in every context.\n\nChanges span all three documentation files:\n- `README.md` — Em spaces in section headings, tables, connection path diagrams, and emblem grid condensed to single-line `<td>` elements\n- `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` — Same treatment across all section headers and table cells\n- `Documentation/GitHub/DeepDive.md` — Consistent enitization for all em-space-delimited headings and component references\n\nAdditionally, condense the multi-line `<td>` sponsor grid in README.md to single-line markup for consistency with the rest of the file. All rendered HTML tables and section headings now display with correct spacing across GitHub, VS Code preview, and standalone renderers.",
			"SHA": "3d1c941efad481ab2f8aa35b36841e2e1d0ccf05"
		}
	],
